\DOC X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC

\TYPE {X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC : thm * (thm option array) -> thm -> term -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Derives a full-procedure {ensures} specification — including stack frame
set-up, callee-saved register restore and return — from a specification of the
procedure core body, either closing the goal outright or leaving one residual
subgoal about the event trace.

\DESCRIBE
{X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff} takes {execth : thm *
(thm option array)}, the machine-code execution package for the program, whose
first component supplies the code length; {coreth : thm}, the specification of
the core body that is lifted to the whole procedure; {reglist : term}, a list
(possibly empty) of callee-saved register components that are saved and
restored; and {stackoff : int}, the size in bytes of the stack frame below the
incoming stack pointer. The goal is a universally quantified {ensures}
statement, optionally under an outer existential (e.g. an event-function
witness), carrying non-overlapping side conditions, with an initial state at
the procedure entry and a final state at the return address with the stack
pointer restored. In most observed traces the goal is discharged completely,
leaving no subgoals. In the remaining traces exactly one subgoal results: the
universal variables and the outer existential witness are instantiated, the
side conditions are stripped into the assumptions in expanded
({nonoverlapping_modulo}) form, and a large set of assumptions describing the
final symbolic state is added — register and flag readings, saved stack slots
holding the initial callee-saved values and the return address, the accumulated
{MAYCHANGE} relation between initial and final state, and the final event list;
the conclusion becomes the remaining existential claim about the event trace.
{
               A ?- t
       ===========================  X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff
         (no goals)
}
{
               A ?- t
       ===========================  X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff
             A, B ?- u
}
\noindent where {B} is the stripped side conditions together with the derived
final-state assumptions, and {u} is the residual trace obligation.

\ENDDOC
